# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A URL's scheme paints as one unit, RFC 3986's own boundary"

# Ruling 2026-09-18 (lar:///url-scheme.paints.free): TextMate's own test — "would I want these
# two elements styled differently?" — says no theme in the surveyed field (VS Code Markdown's
# `markup.underline.link.markdown`, VS Code HTML's attribute strings) scopes a URL's scheme
# apart from its body; RFC 3986 draws the boundary at the first `:` regardless (`//` opens the
# authority only for schemes that carry one). The collision: painting `scheme:` or `scheme://`
# as ONE unit is free on this tree under the bare autolink's OWN name (already per-scheme
# dynamic, `markup.underline.link.external.$1.tiddlywiki5`) and, inside a `[[go|https://…]]` or
# `[ext[https://…]]` target, free under the DIFFERENT paired name
# `entity.name.scheme support.type.scheme` — reusing one identical spelling in both places costs
# 2 floors, so the two locations spell it differently on purpose. `https` sorts before `http` in
# every alternation below.

! A bare autolink keeps its own per-scheme name, widened over the scheme+`://` unit

See https://example.com/a here.
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.https.tiddlywiki5
#         ^ markup.underline.link.external.https.tiddlywiki5
#           ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5
#           ^ - markup.underline.link.external.https.tiddlywiki5

! A scheme without `//` widens only to its own colon; the path is a control — unaffected either way

Mail me at mailto:test@example.com please.
#          ^ markup.underline.link.external.mailto.tiddlywiki5
#                ^ markup.underline.link.external.mailto.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^ markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5
#                 ^ - markup.underline.link.external.mailto.tiddlywiki5

! A captioned pretty link's target scopes its scheme under the paired, differently-spelled name

A [[go|https://example.com]] here.
#      ^ entity.name.scheme.https.tiddlywiki5 support.type.scheme.https.tiddlywiki5
#              ^ string.entity.other.title.link.tiddlywiki5
#              ^ - entity.name.scheme
#              ^ - support.type.scheme

! An `[ext[` target scopes its scheme the same way

An [ext[https://example.com]] here.
#       ^ entity.name.scheme.https.tiddlywiki5 support.type.scheme.https.tiddlywiki5
#               ^ markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5
#               ^ - entity.name.scheme
